00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.780
Yeah, you just get rid of one.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.240
So, I think it'd still be Zexy.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:28.900
Yeah, yeah. Have you guys heard of the mid-2000s movie, Zizix Road?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.100
Absolutely not.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.240
No. Okay, yeah.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:38.700
It's spelled Z-Y-Z-Z-Y-X and then Road.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:47.540
It was released in 2006 and it had Katherine Heigl and Tom Sizemore in it.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:56.080
And I think it's main claim to fame, aside from having an unpronounceable title, is it's box office gross was $30.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:03.300
So, when I started playing this game, I just kept thinking of Zizix Road.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.680
And, like, who came up with this title?

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.860
What was the idea?

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.680
Were they just trying to be at the bottom of all the catalogs because people would slip there?

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.900
It definitely doesn't mean anything.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.080
I feel like you could get to the bottom of all the catalogs without going Zizix.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.340
You could just start with a Z and you're probably at the bottom.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.940
So, that's probably a box office record, too, right?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.680
Or maybe there was a movie that didn't sell any tickets.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.380
I'm sure it's possible.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:44.880
Actually, no. Just looking at Wikipedia right now, apparently, there are other films that have lower grossing movies, like, box office figures.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.820
But that must mean zero, right?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.760
Yeah, it's up to Nostalgia the movie to break the record and make no money whatsoever.

